 },
 "findings_side": {
  "qdrant_idf_modifier_is_per_shard": "PUT a sparse vector with modifier idf on a 2-shard probe collection (3 points, 2 with the sparse vector, one per shard): scores matched IDF computed with each shard's own N and df (term in both points: ln(1+0.5/1.5) = 0.2877 per shard instead of the global ln(1+0.5/2.5)). With 6 shards and all 191,634 titles holding the vector, the modifier would not give the prototype's eligible-corpus IDF, hence client IDF.",
  "undici_40ms_stall": "undici fetch (and Node's global fetch) against Qdrant 1.19 REST on loopback: responses of about 1.1 to 5.5 KB wait ~40 ms (delayed-ACK signature) no matter the query type (dense fingerprint_raw limit 20/50: 39/40 and 40/40 requests stalled; limit 150 = 8 KB: 0/40). connect noDelay does not help. curl, Python http.client and node:http (keep-alive agent, req.end(body)) do not stall. Crate responses do not stall. In bench/replay/out/runs.jsonl best-c1, 166 of 1,008 Qdrant stage requests have wall - server time in 38-60 ms and none in 20-38 ms: the replay's Qdrant times carry this stall too.",
  "adding_vector_reoptimizes": "PUT /points/vectors on every point makes the optimizer rewrite the segments: the collection stayed yellow for 310 s after the 51 s upload"
 },
 "term_stats_client": {
  "source": "bench/sparse/termstats_heap.mjs on out/term_stats_eligible.json",
  "terms_with_eligible_df": 659282,
  "vocab_ids_all_titles": 1548830,
  "json_bytes": 18552615,
  "json_gzip_bytes": 6244980,
  "node_heap_mib": 49.2,
  "idf_float32_by_id_mib": 5.9,
  "load_ms": 699,
  "note": "the webapp needs term -> id for text queries (terms with eligible df > 0 only) and IDF by id for the profile (built from fetched seed vectors); N plus df per term is everything, avglen/k1/b/field weights are needed only by the writer. The full stats including terms seen only in ineligible titles are 44 MB JSON."
 },
 "summary": {
  "parity": "exact: text ops (main 123, coverage 79, mention 49 top-k + 49 score-ids) tie-aware recall 1.0 everywhere, max abs score error 4.2e-6 (max rel 2e-7); document values bitwise equal to sparse.index(BODY); IDF equal. Profile terms: with the prototype's own term selection recall 1.0 and rel error 3.2e-7; with the client's selection 6 of 57 profiles swap terms tied at the 40th weight (numpy argsort tie order), 4 of them change the top-300 list (recall 0.68-0.99).",
  "latency_node_http_c1": "Qdrant total p50/p95: top300 2.59/3.04, top500 2.65/3.06, ids 3.29/4.51 ms (server p50 0.25-0.64); Crate: top300 4.33/8.18, top500 4.39/8.15, ids 5.96/9.93 ms (server p50 1.06-2.60)",
  "latency_node_http_c4": "Qdrant top300 2.87/3.72, top500 2.90/3.81, ids 3.60/5.39; Crate top300 5.34/11.06, top500 5.38/11.92, ids 9.66/14.67",
  "latency_undici": "same p50s, but ~12% of Qdrant top-k and 23% of score-ids requests stall ~40 ms (p95 ~44 ms): a client/transport issue, not the sparse index",
  "size": "disk 415 MiB allocated (index 259, storage 156 of 408 apparent); RAM +440 MiB jemalloc (in-RAM inverted index; storage mmap only paged in when vectors are fetched); 23.4 M nnz over 181,037 titles (41% = 9.7 M on the 50,305 eligible ones); client stats 49 MiB Node heap",
  "drift": "30 days of changes (3,900 titles, all counted as new eligible, newest first): avglen <= 0.9%, stored values <= 0.8%, top-300 recall mean 0.998 / min 0.977 with current IDF. Stale IDF is worse (dropped new terms: recall 0 on some ops by 90 days), so refresh the client stats often and rebuild document values rarely."
